    <div class="case-body">
      <section>
        <h2><span class="pin-name">01</span> The idea</h2>
        <p>
          Online blind tests play everybody's hits. This one plays <b>each player's own</b> music: their most
          played songs, their favourites, their playlists. You hear a snippet, find the artist, the title,
          the album and the year, then challenge your friends on your own taste.
        </p>
        <p>The game itself is in French.</p>
        <figure class="case-figure">
          <BrowserShot src="/images/blindtest.webp" url="github.io/own_blindtest" alt="Blind test home page: choosing where your music comes from" id="blindtest" />
          <figcaption>The home page: first, you choose where your music comes from.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>Three games share the same sources:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <b>Blind test.</b> A 30-second snippet, and questions: artist, title, album, year. In
            <i>Classic</i> mode, the number of songs is set in advance; in <i>Sudden death</i>, the game goes
            on as long as you find the artist or the title. You answer by picking one of 4 options (the
            default on phones), or by typing everything, typos tolerated.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Cover surprise.</b> Five covers from your albums, pixelated, sharper after each of the 6
            tries. Each try gives a hint: the year, the genre, the artist's initials, then a 5-second snippet.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Who listens to this?</b> A multiplayer game, everyone on their own phone. Each player brings
            15 songs, and every round you guess whose song is playing, and which one it is.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2><span class="pin-name">02</span> Where the music comes from</h2>
        <table class="case-table">
