            <tr><th scope="row">Deezer</th><td>The link to your public profile, no password</td><td>Your top songs, favourites and playlists</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">File</th><td>The history Spotify or YouTube Music send on request (ZIP or JSON)</td><td>Your most played songs, since day one</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Spotify</th><td>A Premium account added as a tester</td><td>Your liked songs, tops and playlists</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
          With Deezer and the file, the sound comes from Deezer's public snippets: no account needed, and
          it works on phones. With Spotify, it goes through Spotify's official player, which needs Premium
          on a computer, and Spotify limits this connection to 5 testers.
        </p>
      </section>

