        <ul>
          <li>
            <b>A static site, with no dependencies and no build step.</b> A few JavaScript files served by
            GitHub Pages: nothing to install, whether you play or develop.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>The music sources.</b> Deezer's API does not accept calls from another website, so the game
            uses its JSONP output. Spotify sign-in works without a server, with the OAuth PKCE flow, and the
            game pauses whenever the API asks it to slow down.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>History files are read locally.</b> The ZIP from Spotify or Google is opened in the browser;
            only plays of at least 30 seconds count.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Challenges fit in a link.</b> The game (songs, questions, score) is compressed into the address.
            A friend replays exactly the same songs, with no account and no database. Since the link can come
            from anyone, every value is checked and bounded when it is opened.
          </li>
        </ul>
